{"name":"Morro Bay","hex":"#546b78","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Morro Bay","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A city in San Luis Obispo County, California, United States."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Morro_Bay"}],"entries":[{"title":"Morro Bay, California","blocks":[{"text":"Morro Bay is a seaside city in San Luis Obispo County, California, United States. Located on the Central Coast of California, the town overlooks Morro Bay, a natural embayment with an all-weather, small-craft, commercial and recreational harbor."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/View_of_the_Morro_Bay_Rock%2C_from_the_Black_Hill_trail_copy.jpg/330px-View_of_the_Morro_Bay_Rock%2C_from_the_Black_Hill_trail_copy.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Morro_Bay%2C_California","wikidata":"Q605491"},{"title":"Bay","blocks":[{"text":"A bay is a recessed, coastal body of water that directly connects to a larger main body of water, such as an ocean, a lake, or another bay. A large bay is usually called a gulf, sea, sound, or bight. A cove is a small, circular bay with a narrow entrance. A fjord is an elongated bay formed by glacial action.\nThe term embayment is also used for related features, such as extinct bays or freshwater environments."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/Aerial_photograph_of_Langness_and_the_bay_at_Castletown_13_February_2014_-_geograph.org.uk_-_3847162.jpg/330px-Aerial_photograph_of_Langness_and_the_bay_at_Castletown_13_February_2014_-_geograph.org.uk_-_3847162.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bay","wikidata":"Q39594"},{"title":"Bay (horse)","blocks":[{"text":"Bay is a hair coat color of horses, characterized by a reddish-brown or brown body color with a black point coloration on the mane, tail, ear edges, and lower legs. Bay is one of the most common coat colors in many horse breeds."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/BayMare.jpg/330px-BayMare.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bay_(horse)","wikidata":"Q900906"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Morro_Bay_power_plant_and_North_bay_front_by_Don_Ramey_Logan.jpg/500px-Morro_Bay_power_plant_and_North_bay_front_by_Don_Ramey_Logan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Morro_Bay_power_plant_and_North_bay_front_by_Don_Ramey_Logan.jpg/1280px-Morro_Bay_power_plant_and_North_bay_front_by_Don_Ramey_Logan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Morro_Bay_power_plant_and_North_bay_front_by_Don_Ramey_Logan.jpg/500px-Morro_Bay_power_plant_and_North_bay_front_by_Don_Ramey_Logan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMorro_Bay_power_plant_and_North_bay_front_by_Don_Ramey_Logan.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Morro-Bay-City-Seal.gif/500px-Morro-Bay-City-Seal.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Morro-Bay-City-Seal.gif/500px-Morro-Bay-City-Seal.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMorro-Bay-City-Seal.gif"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/Morro_Rock_-_1883_%282619478125%29.jpg/500px-Morro_Rock_-_1883_%282619478125%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedi